# Prototype .sgm translation of samples/health/patient-vitals.xml.
#
# History: the design doc originally (wrongly) claimed dimension="3" was dead on
# MultivariateNormal; that was corrected to "it's real and required" after this file
# genuinely failed to load without it. That correction has now itself been superseded:
# MultivariateNormal.configure() was a real, fixed bug (DIAGONAL mode didn't infer
# dimension from means/sigmas length the way FULL mode already infers it from covariance's
# row count -- see the class's own updated comment). dimension is omitted below on
# purpose, to prove the fix, not by oversight.

dataset.root = Vitals

Vitals = MultivariateNormal(means=(72, 118, 98), sigmas=(8, 12, 1.5))
